msgid "Scrapy 2.6.2 (2022-07-25)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:4978 ../../../news.rst:5462 ../../../news.rst:6977
#: ../../../news.rst:7074
msgid "**Security bug fix:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:4980 ../../../news.rst:6979
msgid ""
"When :class:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares.httpproxy.HttpProxyMiddleware` "
"processes a request with :reqmeta:`proxy` metadata, and that :reqmeta:"
"`proxy` metadata includes proxy credentials, :class:`~scrapy."
"downloadermiddlewares.httpproxy.HttpProxyMiddleware` sets the ``Proxy-"
"Authorization`` header, but only if that header is not already set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:4987 ../../../news.rst:6986
msgid ""
"There are third-party proxy-rotation downloader middlewares that set "
"different :reqmeta:`proxy` metadata every time they process a request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:4990 ../../../news.rst:6989
msgid ""
"Because of request retries and redirects, the same request can be processed "
"by downloader middlewares more than once, including both :class:`~scrapy."
"downloadermiddlewares.httpproxy.HttpProxyMiddleware` and any third-party "
"proxy-rotation downloader middleware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:4995 ../../../news.rst:6994
msgid ""
"These third-party proxy-rotation downloader middlewares could change the :"
"reqmeta:`proxy` metadata of a request to a new value, but fail to remove the "
"``Proxy-Authorization`` header from the previous value of the :reqmeta:"
"`proxy` metadata, causing the credentials of one proxy to be sent to a "
"different proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5001 ../../../news.rst:7000
msgid ""
"To prevent the unintended leaking of proxy credentials, the behavior of :"
"class:`~scrapy.downloadermiddlewares.httpproxy.HttpProxyMiddleware` is now "
"as follows when processing a request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5005 ../../../news.rst:7004
msgid ""
"If the request being processed defines :reqmeta:`proxy` metadata that "
"includes credentials, the ``Proxy-Authorization`` header is always updated "
"to feature those credentials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5009 ../../../news.rst:7008
msgid ""
"If the request being processed defines :reqmeta:`proxy` metadata without "
"credentials, the ``Proxy-Authorization`` header is removed *unless* it was "
"originally defined for the same proxy URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5013 ../../../news.rst:7012
msgid ""
"To remove proxy credentials while keeping the same proxy URL, remove the "
"``Proxy-Authorization`` header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5016 ../../../news.rst:7015
msgid ""
"If the request has no :reqmeta:`proxy` metadata, or that metadata is a falsy "
"value (e.g. ``None``), the ``Proxy-Authorization`` header is removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5020 ../../../news.rst:7019
msgid ""
"It is no longer possible to set a proxy URL through the :reqmeta:`proxy` "
"metadata but set the credentials through the ``Proxy-Authorization`` header. "
"Set proxy credentials through the :reqmeta:`proxy` metadata instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5025
msgid "Also fixes the following regressions introduced in 2.6.0:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5027
msgid ""
":class:`~scrapy.crawler.CrawlerProcess` supports again crawling multiple "
"spiders (:gh:`5435`, :gh:`5436`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5030
msgid ""
"Installing a Twisted reactor before Scrapy does (e.g. importing :mod:"
"`twisted.internet.reactor` somewhere at the module level) no longer prevents "
"Scrapy from starting, as long as a different reactor is not specified in :"
"setting:`TWISTED_REACTOR` (:gh:`5525`, :gh:`5528`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5035
msgid ""
"Fixed an exception that was being logged after the spider finished under "
"certain conditions (:gh:`5437`, :gh:`5440`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5038
msgid ""
"The ``--output``/``-o`` command-line parameter supports again a value "
"starting with a hyphen (:gh:`5444`, :gh:`5445`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:5041
msgid ""
"The ``scrapy parse -h`` command no longer throws an error (:gh:`5481`, :gh:"
"`5482`)"
msgstr ""

