#: ../../../news.rst:7708
msgid "Selector API changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7710
msgid ""
"While these are not changes in Scrapy itself, but rather in the parsel_ "
"library which Scrapy uses for xpath/css selectors, these changes are worth "
"mentioning here. Scrapy now depends on parsel >= 1.5, and Scrapy "
"documentation is updated to follow recent ``parsel`` API conventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7715
msgid ""
"Most visible change is that ``.get()`` and ``.getall()`` selector methods "
"are now preferred over ``.extract_first()`` and ``.extract()``. We feel that "
"these new methods result in a more concise and readable code. See :ref:`old-"
"extraction-api` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7721
msgid ""
"There are currently **no plans** to deprecate ``.extract()`` and ``."
"extract_first()`` methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7724
msgid ""
"Another useful new feature is the introduction of ``Selector.attrib`` and "
"``SelectorList.attrib`` properties, which make it easier to get attributes "
"of HTML elements. See :ref:`selecting-attributes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7728
msgid ""
"CSS selectors are cached in parsel >= 1.5, which makes them faster when the "
"same CSS path is used many times. This is very common in case of Scrapy "
"spiders: callbacks are usually called several times, on different pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7733
msgid ""
"If you're using custom ``Selector`` or ``SelectorList`` subclasses, a "
"**backward incompatible** change in parsel may affect your code. See `parsel "
"changelog`_ for a detailed description, as well as for the full list of "
"improvements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7741
msgid "Telnet console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7743
msgid ""
"**Backward incompatible**: Scrapy's telnet console now requires username and "
"password. See :ref:`topics-telnetconsole` for more details. This change "
"fixes a **security issue**; see :ref:`release-1.5.2` release notes for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7748
msgid "New extensibility features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7750
msgid ""
"``from_crawler`` support is added to feed exporters and feed storages. This, "
"among other things, allows to access Scrapy settings from custom feed "
"storages and exporters (:gh:`1605`, :gh:`3348`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7753
msgid ""
"``from_crawler`` support is added to dupefilters (:gh:`2956`); this allows "
"to access e.g. settings or a spider from a dupefilter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7755
msgid ""
":signal:`item_error` is fired when an error happens in a pipeline (:gh:"
"`3256`);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7757
msgid ""
":signal:`request_reached_downloader` is fired when Downloader gets a new "
"Request; this signal can be useful e.g. for custom Schedulers (:gh:`3393`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7760
msgid ""
"new SitemapSpider :meth:`~.SitemapSpider.sitemap_filter` method which allows "
"to select sitemap entries based on their attributes in SitemapSpider "
"subclasses (:gh:`3512`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7763
msgid ""
"Lazy loading of Downloader Handlers is now optional; this enables better "
"initialization error handling in custom Downloader Handlers (:gh:`3394`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7767
msgid "New FilePipeline and MediaPipeline features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7769
msgid ""
"Expose more options for S3FilesStore: :setting:`AWS_ENDPOINT_URL`, :setting:"
"`AWS_USE_SSL`, :setting:`AWS_VERIFY`, :setting:`AWS_REGION_NAME`. For "
"example, this allows to use alternative or self-hosted AWS-compatible "
"providers (:gh:`2609`, :gh:`3548`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:7773
msgid ""
"ACL support for Google Cloud Storage: :setting:`FILES_STORE_GCS_ACL` and :"
"setting:`IMAGES_STORE_GCS_ACL` (:gh:`3199`)."
msgstr ""

