#: ../../../news.rst:8579
msgid "This 1.1 release brings a lot of interesting features and bug fixes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8581
msgid ""
"Scrapy 1.1 has beta Python 3 support (requires Twisted >= 15.5). See :ref:"
"`news_betapy3` for more details and some limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8583
msgid "Hot new features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8585
msgid "Item loaders now support nested loaders (:gh:`1467`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8586
msgid "``FormRequest.from_response`` improvements (:gh:`1382`, :gh:`1137`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8587
msgid ""
"Added setting :setting:`AUTOTHROTTLE_TARGET_CONCURRENCY` and improved "
"AutoThrottle docs (:gh:`1324`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8589
msgid "Added ``response.text`` to get body as unicode (:gh:`1730`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8590
msgid "Anonymous S3 connections (:gh:`1358`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8591
msgid ""
"Deferreds in downloader middlewares (:gh:`1473`). This enables better robots."
"txt handling (:gh:`1471`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8593
msgid ""
"HTTP caching now follows RFC2616 more closely, added settings :setting:"
"`HTTPCACHE_ALWAYS_STORE` and :setting:"
"`HTTPCACHE_IGNORE_RESPONSE_CACHE_CONTROLS` (:gh:`1151`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8596
msgid ""
"Selectors were extracted to the parsel_ library (:gh:`1409`). This means you "
"can use Scrapy Selectors without Scrapy and also upgrade the selectors "
"engine without needing to upgrade Scrapy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8599
msgid ""
"HTTPS downloader now does TLS protocol negotiation by default, instead of "
"forcing TLS 1.0. You can also set the SSL/TLS method using the new "
"``DOWNLOADER_CLIENT_TLS_METHOD`` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8603
msgid "These bug fixes may require your attention:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8605
msgid ""
"Don't retry bad requests (HTTP 400) by default (:gh:`1289`). If you need the "
"old behavior, add ``400`` to :setting:`RETRY_HTTP_CODES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8607
msgid ""
"Fix shell files argument handling (:gh:`1710`, :gh:`1550`). If you try "
"``scrapy shell index.html`` it will try to load the URL ``http://index."
"html``, use ``scrapy shell ./index.html`` to load a local file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8610
msgid ""
"Robots.txt compliance is now enabled by default for newly-created projects (:"
"gh:`1724`). Scrapy will also wait for robots.txt to be downloaded before "
"proceeding with the crawl (:gh:`1735`). If you want to disable this "
"behavior, update :setting:`ROBOTSTXT_OBEY` in ``settings.py`` file after "
"creating a new project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8615
msgid ""
"Exporters now work on unicode, instead of bytes by default (:gh:`1080`). If "
"you use :class:`~scrapy.exporters.PythonItemExporter`, you may want to "
"update your code to disable binary mode which is now deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8618
msgid "Accept XML node names containing dots as valid (:gh:`1533`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8619
msgid ""
"When uploading files or images to S3 (with ``FilesPipeline`` or "
"``ImagesPipeline``), the default ACL policy is now \"private\" instead of "
"\"public\" **Warning: backward incompatible!**. You can use :setting:"
"`FILES_STORE_S3_ACL` to change it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8623
msgid ""
"We've reimplemented ``canonicalize_url()`` for more correct output, "
"especially for URLs with non-ASCII characters (:gh:`1947`). This could "
"change link extractors output compared to previous Scrapy versions. This may "
"also invalidate some cache entries you could still have from pre-1.1 runs. "
"**Warning: backward incompatible!**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8629
msgid "Keep reading for more details on other improvements and bug fixes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8634
msgid "Beta Python 3 Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:8636
msgid ""
"We have been hard at work to make Scrapy run on Python 3. As a result, now "
"you can run spiders on Python 3.3, 3.4 and 3.5 (Twisted >= 15.5 required). "
"Some features are still missing (and some may never be ported)."
